# Dynamic Pi Workflow Scale Catalog

Recovered from `workflow_os` run `wfr_mpzlnt6g_6m5ryl` after conversation compaction ate the visible result. The durable workflow record preserved the fan-out findings and synthesis.

## Recovery receipts

- Workflow run: `wfr_mpzlnt6g_6m5ryl`
- Workflow name: `dynamic-workflow-catalog-research`
- Status: `completed`
- Agents: 7 total, 7 done, 0 failed
- Original recovered branches: `cloudflare-primitives`, `durable-workflow-engines`, `xstate-state-machines`, `event-use-cases`, `catalog-synthesis`
- Original missing/blank branches in persisted run: `agent-orchestration`, `catalog-verifier`
- Follow-up completed on 2026-06-04: verified research for LangGraph, OpenAI Agents/Responses, Vercel AI SDK, Claude Code/HITL/audit/memory/security, and Trigger.dev durable tasks was accepted and persisted into this note.
- Remaining follow-up caveat: one branch output was blank and is not treated as research evidence.

Caveat: the agent orchestration material below is **pattern vocabulary**, not a runtime commitment. The production spine stays: XState lifecycle truth, Zod artifact contracts, Durable Object capsule supervision, pinned Artifacts receipts, brokered secret leases, verification contracts, and Wzrrd/Brain review/output surfaces.

## 1. Executive read

“Infinitely scalable” is the wrong promise. Call it:

> **unbounded addressability with bounded hot concurrency**

We can address huge numbers of context capsules, Artifacts repos, queued lanes, D1 rows, R2 blobs, and sleeping workflow instances. We cannot run infinite hot sandboxes. Active work is bounded by Cloudflare quotas, container vCPU/memory/disk, Workers CPU/subrequests, Queues throughput, model/API rate limits, secret lease limits, token budgets, and cost.

Receipts:

- Cloudflare Workflows are finite: 50k concurrent instances, 2M queued, 300 creations/sec/account, 1 MB event payload, 1 GB persisted state. Source: [Limits · Cloudflare Workflows docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/reference/limits/)
- Cloudflare Containers are finite: paid account live caps include 1,500 vCPU, 6 TiB memory, 30 TB disk. Source: [Limits and Instance Types · Cloudflare Containers docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/containers/platform-details/limits/)
- XState actors process events one at a time and are not a durable or bounded queue. Sources: [Actors · Stately docs](https://stately.ai/docs/actors), [`Mailbox.ts` · XState source](https://github.com/statelyai/xstate/blob/main/packages/core/src/Mailbox.ts)

Sharp architecture line:

```txt
many durable capsules/repos/runs
+ tiny bounded active sandbox slots
+ explicit admission/backpressure
+ replay from Artifacts + snapshots/events
```

For this repo, the current local docs already agree: `docs/dynamic-workflow-machine.md` says plan/machine/verification artifacts must be pinned before sandbox creation, and `.brain/projects/pi-sandbox-workflows.svx` says **capsule ID beats sandbox ID**.

Deployed prototype receipt: `prototypes/cloudflare-parallel-workflow-spike/` ran `run-parallel-cloudflare-patterns-3e945e7e-887dd5a9` through Worker + Durable Object + Queue + Sandbox + Artifacts with 8 planned lanes, concurrency cap 3, max observed active lanes 3, final state `captured`, verifier `verified`, and all lane/synthesis/verifier/delivery sandboxes destroyed with `:ok`.

## 2. Pattern catalog

### Lifecycle patterns

#### Plan-pin-before-run

Sources: [How Artifacts works · Cloudflare Artifacts docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/concepts/how-artifacts-works/), [Best practices for Artifacts · Cloudflare Artifacts docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/concepts/best-practices/), local `docs/dynamic-workflow-machine.md`.

Shape:

```txt
idle
→ resolvingCapsule
→ selectingContextPacks
→ generatingPlan
→ validatingPlan
→ committingPlanArtifacts
→ queuedForExecution
```

Events:

```txt
RUN_REQUESTED
CAPSULE_RESOLVED
CONTEXT_PACK_SELECTED
PLAN_GENERATED
PLAN_REJECTED
PLAN_PINNED
```

Pi implication: commit before sandbox creation:

```txt
run/plan.json
workflows/machine.ts
workflows/harness.js
run/verification-contract.json
run/manifest.json
```

If the plan is not pinned first, the run is not auditable enough to trust.

#### Sandbox lease lifecycle

Sources: [Sandbox lifecycle · Cloudflare Sandbox SDK docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/sandbox/concepts/sandboxes/), [Limits · Cloudflare Sandbox SDK docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/sandbox/platform/limits/), [Security model · Cloudflare Sandbox SDK docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/sandbox/concepts/security/).

Shape:

```txt
awaitingSlot
→ mintingSecretLeases
→ attachingSandbox
→ hydratingWorkspace
→ runningLane
→ committingOutputs
→ destroyingSandbox
→ laneCaptured
```

Events:

```txt
SLOT_GRANTED
SECRET_LEASES_MINTED
SANDBOX_READY
WORKSPACE_HYDRATED
LANE_SUCCEEDED
OUTPUTS_COMMITTED
SANDBOX_DESTROYED
```

Pi implication: sandbox ID is disposable compute. Durable state goes to Artifacts/R2/D1/DO, not `/workspace`.

### Scaling and backpressure patterns

#### Admission + quota broker

Sources: [Limits · Cloudflare Queues docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/queues/platform/limits/), [Batching, Retries and Delays · Cloudflare Queues docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/queues/configuration/batching-retries/), [Delivery guarantees · Cloudflare Queues docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/queues/reference/delivery-guarantees/).

Shape:

```txt
runRequested
→ checkingCapsuleLock
→ checkingQuota
→ admitted | queued | rejected | dlq
```

Events:

```txt
RUN_REQUESTED
CAPSULE_LOCKED
QUOTA_GRANTED
QUOTA_DENIED
QUEUE_ENQUEUED
DLQ_WRITTEN
```

Backpressure:

- Queue ingress work.
- Durable Object owns capsule lock.
- D1 indexes budget/quota status.
- Every queue handler is idempotent because Queues are at least once.

Pi implication: DO admits only when sandbox/model/token/secret budgets allow. Waiting lanes hold no container.

#### Bounded fan-out/fan-in

Sources: [Concurrency management · Inngest Documentation](https://www.inngest.com/docs/guides/concurrency), [Concurrency & Queues · Trigger.dev](https://trigger.dev/docs/queue-concurrency), [Step Functions service quotas · AWS Step Functions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/service-quotas.html).

Shape:

```txt
planningLanes
→ waitingForSlot
→ runningLane[]
→ fanIn
→ aggregateVerification
→ captured
```

Events:

```txt
LANE_PLANNED
SLOT_GRANTED
SLOT_DENIED
LANE_STARTED
LANE_OUTPUT_COMMITTED
LANE_FAILED
ALL_LANES_SETTLED
FANIN_READY
```

Rule: address thousands of lanes, run only `N` hot sandboxes.

Pi implication: use spawned XState actors for dynamic lanes, but cap before spawn. Active slots are leased by supervisor policy, not by optimistic JavaScript loops.

Prototype receipt: the deployed `cloudflare-parallel-workflow-spike` fixture planned 8 lanes, capped hot concurrency at 3, observed max active lanes of 3, committed all 8 lane outputs to Artifacts, then fan-in/synthesis/verifier/delivery completed to `captured`.

### Coordination patterns

#### Capsule supervisor actor

Sources: [Rules of Durable Objects · Cloudflare Durable Objects docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/best-practices/rules-of-durable-objects/), [Limits · Cloudflare Durable Objects docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/platform/limits/), [Actors · Stately docs](https://stately.ai/docs/actors).

Shape:

```txt
idle
→ resolvingCapsule
→ pinningContextPacks
→ committingPlanArtifacts
→ acquiringBudgetSlot
→ runningLanes
→ verifying
→ deliveringOutput
→ cleanup
→ captured
```

Events:

```txt
START_REQUEST
CAPSULE_RESOLVED
PLAN_ARTIFACTS_COMMITTED
BUDGET_SLOT_GRANTED
LANE_DONE
VERIFICATION_ACCEPTED
OUTPUT_PUBLISHED
CANCEL_REQUESTED
REPLAY_REQUESTED
```

Pi implication: one Durable Object per `contextCapsuleId`, not one global coordinator. The DO owns lifecycle truth, current XState snapshot, event log pointer, locks, cancellation, active lane refs, and Wzrrd/Brain review state.

#### Child workflow / lane workflow

Sources: [Child Workflows · Temporal docs](https://docs.temporal.io/child-workflows), [Workflow · Convex component](https://www.convex.dev/components/workflow), [client.trigger · Upstash Documentation](https://upstash.com/docs/workflow/basics/client/trigger).

Use when a lane has:

- its own retry/cancel lifecycle
- long history
- separate worker profile
- independent verification/output

Pi implication: parent capsule workflow owns policy and fan-in. Child lane workflow owns one sandbox run and returns Artifacts refs, not giant payloads.

### Reliability patterns

#### Durable step as transaction

Sources: [Rules of Workflows · Cloudflare Workflows docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/rules-of-workflows/), [Sleeping and retrying · Cloudflare Workflows docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/sleeping-and-retrying/), [Inngest Steps · Inngest Documentation](https://www.inngest.com/docs/learn/inngest-steps).

Shape:

```txt
scheduled
→ running
→ succeeded | failed
→ retry_wait
→ running | terminal_failed
```

Events:

```txt
STEP_SCHEDULED
STEP_STARTED
STEP_SUCCEEDED
STEP_FAILED
RETRY_TIMER_FIRED
NON_RETRYABLE_ERROR
```

Pi implication: one side-effect boundary per step:

- resolve capsule
- pin plan
- mint leases
- create sandbox
- hydrate workspace
- run Pi
- commit outputs
- verify
- publish review
- cleanup

Step output should be refs: `artifactCommit`, `leaseRef`, `sandboxRunId`, `verificationResultRef`.

#### Cancel/cleanup

Sources: [Workers API · Cloudflare Workflows docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/workers-api/), [Promise actors · Stately docs](https://stately.ai/docs/promise-actors), [Callback Actors · Stately docs](https://stately.ai/docs/callback-actors).

Shape:

```txt
running
→ cancelling
→ terminatingWorkflow
→ destroyingSandbox
→ revokingLeases
→ cancelled
```

Events:

```txt
CANCEL_REQUESTED
WORKFLOW_TERMINATED
SANDBOX_DESTROYED
LEASE_REVOKED
CLEANUP_DONE
```

Pi implication: cancel means stop new work, kill/close active work where possible, destroy sandbox, revoke leases, and record a cancellation receipt. Already-started external side effects need idempotency/compensation.

#### Replay/repair

Sources: [Persistence · Stately docs](https://stately.ai/docs/persistence), [Events and Event History · Temporal docs](https://docs.temporal.io/workflow-execution/event), [Restarting state machine executions with redrive in Step Functions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/redrive-executions.html).

Shape:

```txt
loadingReceipt
→ restoringSnapshot | restartingFromStep
→ rerunningLane | rerunningVerifier
→ verifying
→ captured | blocked
```

Events:

```txt
REPLAY_REQUESTED
SNAPSHOT_RESTORED
STEP_REDRIVEN
VERIFICATION_PASSED
VERIFICATION_BLOCKED
```

Pi implication: use XState snapshot for operational resume; use event log + Artifacts commits for audit replay. Restored XState snapshots do not re-run actions, but invoked work can restart, so every side-effecting actor needs idempotency checks.

### Human/review patterns

#### Durable interruption / approval gate

Sources: [Events and parameters · Cloudflare Workflows docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/build/events-and-parameters/), [Wait for token · Trigger.dev](https://trigger.dev/docs/wait-for-token), [OpenAI guardrails and approvals](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents/guardrails-approvals), [LangGraph interrupts](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langgraph/interrupts), [Temporal human-in-the-loop AI agent](https://docs.temporal.io/ai-cookbook/human-in-the-loop-python), local `prototypes/review-gate-spike/src/run.ts`.

Shape:

```txt
running | toolProposed | verificationNeedsHuman
→ approvalPayloadPinned
→ pendingHumanReview
→ approved | edited | rejected | timedOut | cancelled
→ deliveringOutput | blocked | cleanup
```

Events:

```txt
APPROVAL_REQUESTED
APPROVAL_PAYLOAD_PINNED
APPROVAL_TOKEN_CREATED
REVIEW_RENDERED
HUMAN_APPROVED
HUMAN_EDITED
HUMAN_REJECTED
WAIT_TIMEOUT
CANCEL_REQUESTED
```

Pi implication:

- The approval binds to an exact action payload hash plus artifact refs, not “approve this agent generally.”
- The capsule Durable Object owns pending approval state, timeout, cancel, and resume routing.
- Wzrrd/Brain render the review surface and return approval/edit/reject events; they are not lifecycle truth.
- `run/approval.json` or equivalent Artifacts receipts should include the redacted payload, hash, verification status, output target, and approval ref.
- Worker sandboxes should be destroyed or slept before long waits. Resume from capsule state and pinned Artifacts, not from a hot shell.
- Public Wzrrd/Artifacts payloads must redact private claim URLs, wait tokens, approval URLs, raw secrets, and bearer-ish callback material.

Mutating external actions wait here unless the verification contract explicitly allows automatic delivery.

### Agent-specific patterns

#### Dynamic harness as pinned artifact

Sources: [A harness for every task: dynamic workflows in Claude Code · Anthropic](https://claude.com/blog/a-harness-for-every-task-dynamic-workflows-in-claude-code), local `.brain/projects/pi-sandbox-workflows.svx`, local `docs/dynamic-workflow-machine.md`.

Shape:

```txt
intent
→ generateHarness
→ validateHarnessPolicy
→ pinHarness
→ executeTrustedRunner
```

Events:

```txt
HARNESS_GENERATED
HARNESS_POLICY_PASSED
HARNESS_POLICY_FAILED
HARNESS_PINNED
EXECUTION_STARTED
```

Pi implication: generated harnesses can define fan-out, phases, stop conditions, verifier roles, and output targets. They do **not** get to widen auth, pick arbitrary context packs, or control their own sandbox lifecycle.

For now, generated `workflows/machine.ts` and `workflows/harness.js` are receipts until policy validation is real. The trusted Worker/supervisor executes known patterns and pins the generated artifacts for review.

### Agent orchestration patterns

Follow-up completed on 2026-06-04 accepted LangGraph, OpenAI Agents/Responses, Vercel AI SDK, Claude Code, Trigger.dev, and HITL/audit/memory/security research as source-backed pattern input. Use these as reusable shapes; do not let vendor ergonomics erase the repo invariant: **unbounded addressability with bounded hot concurrency**.

#### Runtime-fit matrix

| Source family | Strongest reusable pattern | Runtime stance | Pi mapping |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| LangGraph | graph state, node boundaries, super-step checkpoints, `interrupt()`, `Send()`/reducers, replay/fork vocabulary | pattern source, not Cloudflare supervisor runtime yet | XState/DO owns lifecycle; Artifacts/event logs own audit; node side effects must be idempotent |
| OpenAI Agents/Responses | bounded agent run loop, item-based function calls, `call_id` tool results, guardrails/approvals, background responses, harness-vs-sandbox split | worker-lane runtime candidate, not supervisor | model lane refs only; tool calls become audit events; OpenAI IDs are not canonical memory |
| Vercel AI SDK | typed tool-loop lane, hard step caps, `prepareStep`, approval parts, subagent compaction, resumable streams | worker/UI lane runtime candidate with version pinning | stop conditions in manifest; stream IDs are UI projections; supervisor owns cancellation |
| Claude Code | dynamic harness source, hooks, permissions, security posture | pattern source for harness receipts and tool gates | generated harness is pinned; `PreToolUse`/permission shapes inform Pi tool audit extensions |
| Trigger.dev | durable task states, queues/concurrency, `batchTriggerAndWait`, wait tokens, idempotency, metadata/streams | workflow vocabulary; AI Chat remains RC unless pinned | scheduled lanes, cold HITL waits, idempotent child runs, artifact-ref fan-in |
| Cross-cutting | HITL, tool audit, secret leases, memory compaction, sandbox boundary | supervisor-enforced policy, not library magic | capsule DO + XState + Zod + Artifacts + leases + Wzrrd/Brain |

#### Pattern card contract

Every reusable workflow pattern should be saved as a card with this minimum shape:

```txt
name
source receipts
states
transitions/events
waits and external callbacks
retry/timeout policy
cancel/cleanup behavior
replay/repair behavior
backpressure and concurrency cap
HITL gates
observability events
memory/compaction boundary
sandbox boundary
Pi mapping: capsule, supervisor, worker lane, artifacts, leases, verifier, output target
version/API caveats
```

This keeps pattern reuse boring enough to validate and render. The card is vocabulary; the executable truth remains the pinned XState machine/harness plus Zod contracts.

#### LangGraph graph/checkpoint/interrupt vocabulary

Sources: [LangGraph JS Graph API](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langgraph/graph-api), [LangGraph JS persistence](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langgraph/persistence), [LangGraph JS durable execution](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langgraph/durable-execution), [LangGraph JS interrupts](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langgraph/interrupts), [LangGraph JS subgraphs](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langgraph/use-subgraphs), [LangGraph JS workflows and agents](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langgraph/workflows-agents), [LangGraphJS Cloudflare Worker checkpointer issue](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraphjs/issues/1692).

Shape:

```txt
stateSnapshot
→ runningNode
→ checkpointingSuperstep
→ routingNext
→ runningNode | pendingHumanReview | fanIn | captured | blocked
```

Events:

```txt
NODE_STARTED
NODE_SUCCEEDED
NODE_FAILED
CHECKPOINT_WRITTEN
ROUTE_SELECTED
INTERRUPT_RAISED
STATE_FORKED
REPLAY_REQUESTED
```

Pi mapping:

- LangGraph `State` maps to Zod-validated `run/manifest.json` plus XState context, not a replacement for either.
- `Command(update, goto)` maps cleanly to XState events with payloads.
- `Send()`/reducers map to scheduled worker lanes and reducer payloads that are artifact refs, not huge model text blobs.
- `interrupt()` maps to the durable approval gate above; resume comes back as a capsule event.
- Subgraphs are useful vocabulary, but opaque subagent-as-tool calls are worse than explicit lane actors with artifact refs and event receipts.
- Checkpoints happen at super-step boundaries; if a node reruns, side effects must be idempotent.

Caveats: do not use LangGraph checkpointers as audit truth, do not rely on in-process concurrency for Cloudflare quotas, and do not allow graph topology/code drift for replayable production runs unless `workflows/machine.ts`, `workflows/harness.js`, and manifest refs were pinned before execution.

#### OpenAI Agents/Responses bounded worker lane

Sources: [OpenAI Agents running agents](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents/running-agents), [OpenAI Agents orchestration](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents/orchestration), [OpenAI guardrails and approvals](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents/guardrails-approvals), [OpenAI sandboxes](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/agents/sandboxes), [OpenAI background mode](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/background), [OpenAI compaction](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/compaction), [OpenAI function calling](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/function-calling), [OpenAI MCP/connectors](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/tools-connectors-mcp).

Shape:

```txt
preparingLaneInput
→ runningModel
→ handlingFunctionCalls
→ submittingToolOutputs
→ maybeHandingOff
→ waitingForBackgroundResponse
→ finalizing
→ workerDone | approvalRequired | failed
```

Events:

```txt
RUN_REQUESTED
MODEL_OUTPUT_RECEIVED
FUNCTION_CALLS_EMITTED
TOOL_OUTPUTS_SUBMITTED
HANDOFF_SELECTED
BACKGROUND_RESPONSE_QUEUED
BACKGROUND_RESPONSE_COMPLETED
FINAL_OUTPUT_READY
MAX_TURNS_EXCEEDED
```

Pi mapping:

- Treat an OpenAI SDK run as one bounded worker lane. The capsule supervisor still owns admission, budget, retries, cancellation, verification, artifact capture, and cleanup.
- Function-call items give a clean audit pair: `function_call { name, arguments, call_id }` and `function_call_output { call_id, output }`.
- Handoffs change lane ownership inside a run; agents-as-tools keep the manager/supervisor lane in control. Prefer agents-as-tools for verifier/report helper lanes unless ownership truly changes.
- `previous_response_id`, conversation IDs, and background response IDs are lane refs only. Canonical memory remains capsule Artifacts, event logs, transcripts, verifier results, and Brain decisions.
- OpenAI sandbox docs reinforce the split this repo already wants: harness/control plane outside, sandbox compute inside.

Caveats: background responses and vendor conversations have retention/compatibility implications; they are not replay receipts. Remote MCP servers are untrusted tool providers and OpenAI warns they can exfiltrate sensitive context, so use allowed-tools policy, approvals, and secret leases.

#### Vercel AI SDK tool-loop lane

Sources: [AI SDK tool calling](https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/ai-sdk-core/tools-and-tool-calling), [AI SDK loop control](https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/agents/loop-control), [AI SDK ToolLoopAgent](https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/reference/ai-sdk-core/tool-loop-agent), [AI SDK workflows](https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/agents/workflows), [AI SDK subagents](https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/agents/subagents), [AI SDK UI tool approvals](https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/ai-sdk-ui/chatbot-tool-usage), [AI SDK resumable streams](https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/ai-sdk-ui/chatbot-resume-streams), [AI SDK telemetry](https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/ai-sdk-core/telemetry), [`tool-loop-agent.ts` source](https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/agent/tool-loop-agent.ts).

Shape:

```txt
modelStep
→ toolCallsAvailable
→ executeTools
→ appendToolResults
→ nextModelStep
→ stopConditionMet | approvalRequired | failed
→ workerDone
```

Events:

```txt
STEP_STARTED
TOOL_CALLS_AVAILABLE
TOOL_EXECUTION_STARTED
TOOL_EXECUTION_FINISHED
STEP_FINISHED
STOP_CONDITION_MET
APPROVAL_REQUIRED
STREAM_RESUME_REQUESTED
```

Pi mapping:

- Use `ToolLoopAgent`/`generateText`/`streamText` style loops as worker lanes, never as the supervisor.
- Pin `stopWhen`/step cap, active tool set, phase gates, and done-tool contract into `run/manifest.json` and `run/verification-contract.json`.
- `prepareStep` maps to supervisor-selected phase gates like `searchOnly → analyzeOnly → summarizeOnly`; workers should not self-widen tools or context.
- A `done`/`finalAnswer` tool means `workerDone → verifying`, not “truth.” It should return structured artifact refs and claim lists.
- Resumable streams are UI projections over run events. `stop()` as client disconnect is not lifecycle cancellation; capsule DO/XState owns cancellation.
- Subagent context offload is useful when the parent sees compact results while full traces go to Artifacts.

Caveat: API names are moving. Docs/source have shown `stepCountIs` vs `isStepCount`, and `needsApproval` vs `toolApproval` depending on Core/ToolLoopAgent/WorkflowAgent. Pin the installed `ai` version before copying snippets.

#### Claude Code hooks, permissions, and harness discipline

Sources: [Claude Code hooks](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks), [Claude Code hooks guide](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks-guide), [Claude Agent SDK permissions](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/permissions), [Claude Code security](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/security), [A harness for every task · Anthropic](https://claude.com/blog/a-harness-for-every-task-dynamic-workflows-in-claude-code).

Shape:

```txt
toolProposed
→ preToolUsePolicy
→ allowed | blocked | permissionRequested
→ toolExecuted
→ postToolBatchAudited
→ nextModelTurn
```

Events:

```txt
PRE_TOOL_USE
TOOL_POLICY_ALLOWED
TOOL_POLICY_BLOCKED
PERMISSION_REQUESTED
TOOL_EXECUTED
POST_TOOL_BATCH_AUDITED
```

Pi mapping:

- Claude Code’s hook/permission vocabulary maps directly to a project-local Pi tool-audit extension: intercept tool calls before execution, redact/annotate results after execution, and persist event rows.
- Permissions approve concrete tool/action shapes; they should not grant hidden broad authority to generated harnesses.
- Dynamic harnesses are valuable for task-specific fan-out, adversarial verification, tournaments, loops, and classification, but the harness must be pinned and policy-checked before execution.
- Claude Code security guidance reinforces the need to treat repo content, tool output, and MCP/tool descriptions as untrusted input.

Caveat: post-tool auditing cannot undo damage. Side-effecting tools need pre-execution policy and, when needed, the durable approval gate.

#### Trigger.dev durable task and AI-session vocabulary

Sources: [Trigger.dev tasks](https://trigger.dev/docs/tasks/overview), [Trigger.dev runs](https://trigger.dev/docs/runs), [Trigger.dev triggering](https://trigger.dev/docs/triggering), [Trigger.dev queue concurrency](https://trigger.dev/docs/queue-concurrency), [Trigger.dev wait for token](https://trigger.dev/docs/wait-for-token), [Trigger.dev idempotency](https://trigger.dev/docs/idempotency), [Trigger.dev errors/retrying](https://trigger.dev/docs/errors-retrying), [Trigger.dev streams](https://trigger.dev/docs/tasks/streams), [Trigger.dev AI Chat overview](https://trigger.dev/docs/ai-chat/overview), [Trigger.dev persistence and replay](https://trigger.dev/docs/ai-chat/patterns/persistence-and-replay), [Trigger.dev tool result auditing](https://trigger.dev/docs/ai-chat/patterns/tool-result-auditing).

Run shape:

```txt
pendingVersion | delayed | queued | dequeued
→ executing
→ waiting
→ executing
→ completed | canceled | failed | timedOut | crashed | systemFailure | expired
```

Fan-out shape:

```txt
planningLanes
→ batchCreated
→ childrenQueued
→ waitingForChildren
→ aggregateResults
→ verifyAggregate
→ captured | blocked
```

Events:

```txt
TASK_TRIGGERED
VERSION_LOCKED
RUN_DEQUEUED
ATTEMPT_STARTED
WAITPOINT_REACHED
WAITPOINT_COMPLETED
BATCH_CREATED
CHILD_RUN_OK
CHILD_RUN_FAILED
ALL_CHILDREN_FINISHED
RETRY_SCHEDULED
CANCEL_REQUESTED
RUN_REPLAY_REQUESTED
```

Pi mapping:

- Use Trigger’s states as durable-workflow vocabulary while XState/DO remains this repo’s lifecycle truth.
- `batchTriggerAndWait` maps to scheduled worker lanes with child outputs as artifact refs.
- Wait tokens map cleanly to Wzrrd/Brain review pages plus capsule-owned pending state.
- Idempotency keys should be deterministic: `capsuleId + runId + stepId + artifactRef` for sandbox creation, Artifacts commits, secret leases, Wzrrd publish, GitHub/Linear/customer mutations.
- Metadata/streams are live projections. Durable memory stays in Artifacts/Brain/event logs.

Caveats: Trigger AI Chat is release-candidate pattern vocabulary until a specific SDK version is pinned. Trigger replay using latest code is not acceptable for audit replay unless the operator explicitly requests redrive-on-latest.

#### Shared tool audit + secret gate

Sources: OpenAI function calling/approvals, Claude Code hooks/permissions, Trigger tool result auditing, Cloudflare Sandbox security, Cloudflare Artifacts best practices, local `docs/kody-secrets-pattern.md`.

Shape:

```txt
toolCallProposed
→ policyPreflight
→ allowed | blocked | needsHumanReview
→ secretLeaseMinted
→ sandboxToolExecution
→ toolResultRecorded
→ leaseRevoked | leaseExpired
```

Events:

```txt
TOOL_CALL_PROPOSED
TOOL_POLICY_ALLOWED
TOOL_POLICY_BLOCKED
TOOL_REVIEW_REQUIRED
SECRET_REF_REQUESTED
SECRET_LEASE_MINTED
TOOL_RESULT_RECORDED
SECRET_LEASE_REVOKED
```

Pi mapping:

- Supervisor validates the allowed tool surface from `run/manifest.json` before any worker sees tools.
- Plans carry `secretRef`, not plaintext. Broker mints task-scoped material only when policy allows it.
- Store `toolCallId`/`call_id`, tool name, actor profile, args hash, redacted args ref, result ref, approval ref, lease refs, duration, and verifier status.
- Secret-bearing network calls should prefer a broker/gateway that injects credentials server-side; only materialize `/workspace/.pi/agent/auth.json` when unavoidable.
- Tool outputs and tool descriptions are untrusted content. Do not let reader lanes write shared Brain or widen secrets.

#### Shared event JSONL contract

Minimum durable event row:

```json
{
  "schemaVersion": "piwf.event.v0",
  "ts": "2026-06-04T00:00:00.000Z",
  "seq": 1,
  "capsuleId": "capsule:external-work-item",
  "runId": "run-abc",
  "laneId": "lane-reader-1",
  "state": "policyPreToolGate",
  "event": "TOOL_CALL_PROPOSED",
  "actor": "worker:reader",
  "payloadHash": "sha256:...",
  "payloadRef": "artifacts://repo/run/events/0001.json",
  "artifactRefs": [],
  "leaseRefs": [],
  "approvalRef": null,
  "verificationRef": null,
  "redaction": "public-safe"
}
```

Persist hot snapshot/status projection in DO/D1. Commit cold receipts to Artifacts as `run/events.jsonl`, traces/log refs, verifier results, and output-delivery receipts. Wzrrd renders from refs; Brain captures reusable decisions after verification.

#### Memory, compaction, and replay boundary

Sources: [OpenAI compaction](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/compaction), [LangGraph persistence](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langgraph/persistence), [Trigger.dev persistence and replay](https://trigger.dev/docs/ai-chat/patterns/persistence-and-replay), [XState persistence](https://stately.ai/docs/persistence), local Pi `docs/compaction.md` and `docs/session-format.md` receipts.

Shape:

```txt
beforeCompaction
→ memoryArtifactWritten
→ memoryVerified
→ compacted
→ restoredFromArtifact
```

Events:

```txt
COMPACTION_REQUESTED
MEMORY_ARTIFACT_PINNED
MEMORY_VERIFICATION_PASSED
MEMORY_VERIFICATION_BLOCKED
COMPACTION_COMPLETED
RESTORE_REQUESTED
```

Pi mapping:

- Runtime context = selected context pack refs, policy, budget, output target, and secret refs.
- Run state = XState snapshot/context plus lane working state.
- Long-term store = Brain, Artifacts, D1 indexes, and R2 blobs; not vendor conversation memory.
- Compaction summaries are model-context helpers until pinned and verified as artifacts.
- Audit replay uses Artifacts commits + event JSONL. Operational resume uses XState snapshots in the control plane.

#### Brain persistence as a terminal workflow step

Source: this follow-up run `wfr_mpzmh6oj_l8zzeo`, Joel's 2026-06-04 correction, and the project Brain rule that durable research belongs in `.brain/` after verification.

Shape:

```txt
verificationAccepted
→ synthesizingDurableMemory
→ writingBrainResource
→ runningBrainCheck
→ verifyingNotesRoute
→ captured
```

Events:

```txt
BRAIN_PERSISTENCE_REQUESTED
BRAIN_NOTE_UPDATED
BRAIN_CHECK_PASSED
NOTES_ROUTE_VERIFIED
PERSISTENCE_BLOCKED
```

Pi mapping:

- Parallel research lanes do not each edit Brain. They return source-backed findings and caveats.
- A single-writer persistence step merges accepted findings into the project Brain note and records remaining gaps.
- The workflow is not “done” until Brain check passes and the local notes route is verified.
- Final output includes file path, Document Host URL, checks run, and uncommitted status.

This prevents the exact failure mode that created this note: good research trapped in workflow output or compacted transcript sludge instead of durable project memory.

#### Generated machine / harness policy validator checklist

Before executing any generated machine or harness as more than receipt-only, require:

- Pattern selected from approved library, or human-reviewed new pattern card.
- `workflows/machine.ts`, `workflows/harness.js`, `run/manifest.json`, `run/verification-contract.json`, and `run/plan.json` pinned before sandbox creation.
- Tool surface declared per lane and denied by default outside the manifest.
- Context pack refs immutable and selected by supervisor, not worker discovery.
- Secret refs declared; no plaintext in plan/harness/events/Wzrrd/Artifacts.
- Budget/stop conditions/retry/timeouts/cancel/cleanup states present.
- Output target explicit: Wzrrd, GitHub, Linear, artifact-only, email draft, etc.
- Verification contract states what blocks capture vs warnings vs HITL.
- Event schema version declared and redaction mode set.
- Sandbox lifecycle includes destroy/sleep receipt on success, failure, timeout, and cancel.

#### API churn and dependency caveats

- Vercel AI SDK docs/source are moving; pin package version before copying `stepCountIs`/`isStepCount`, `needsApproval`/`toolApproval`, or WorkflowAgent examples.
- OpenAI Sandbox Agents are beta pattern vocabulary; OpenAI background/conversation state is lane continuation, not audit memory.
- Trigger.dev AI Chat is RC pattern vocabulary unless a specific `@trigger.dev/sdk` version is pinned.
- LangGraphJS Cloudflare Worker checkpointer support has an open issue; do not build production Cloudflare supervision on it yet.
- Remote MCP/tool servers can exfiltrate context. Treat them as untrusted and require allowed tools, approval gates, and secret leases.

### Observability patterns

#### Event/snapshot/status indexing

Sources: [Inspection · Stately docs](https://stately.ai/docs/inspection), [Metrics and analytics · Cloudflare Workflows docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workflows/observability/metrics-analytics/), [Diagnostics in Durable Functions · Azure](https://docs.azure.cn/en-us/azure-functions/durable-functions/durable-functions-diagnostics).

Persist:

```txt
@xstate.event      → run/events.jsonl
@xstate.snapshot   → DO/D1 status projection
@xstate.actor      → lane registry
@xstate.microstep  → policy/debug trace
```

Index fields:

```txt
capsuleId
externalWorkItemId
workflowId
runId
state
laneId
provider
sandboxId
artifactRepo
artifactCommit
contextPackRefs
leaseRefs
verificationStatus
wzrrdUrl
failureKind
retryCount
costBucket
quotaBucket
```

Pi implication: D1 is query/index. Artifacts are receipts. R2 is bulky evidence. Wzrrd/Brain are human-readable review.

### Security/secrets patterns

#### Secret leases, not raw secrets

Sources: [Manage account secrets · Cloudflare Secrets Store docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/secrets-store/manage-secrets/), [Workers integration · Cloudflare Secrets Store docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/secrets-store/integrations/workers/), local `docs/kody-secrets-pattern.md`.

Shape:

```txt
requestSecretRefs
→ checkPolicy
→ mintLease
→ materializeTaskAuth
→ revokeOrExpire
```

Events:

```txt
SECRET_REF_REQUESTED
SECRET_POLICY_APPROVED
SECRET_POLICY_DENIED
LEASE_MINTED
LEASE_EXPIRED
LEASE_REVOKED
```

Pi implication: plans contain `secretRef`, never plaintext. Broker materializes task-scoped `/workspace/.pi/agent/auth.json`. Public Artifacts/Wzrrd/event logs carry lease metadata only.

### Artifact/memory patterns

#### Git-native durable workspace

Sources: [How Artifacts works · Cloudflare Artifacts docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/concepts/how-artifacts-works/), [Sandbox SDK + Artifacts · Cloudflare Artifacts docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/examples/sandbox-sdk-artifacts/), [Limits · Cloudflare Artifacts docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/platform/limits/).

Store in Artifacts:

```txt
run/plan.json
run/manifest.json
run/verification-contract.json
workflows/machine.ts
workflows/harness.js
context-packs/**
artifacts/reports/**
artifacts/verification/**
transcripts/**
patches/**
```

Pi implication: Artifacts is the reviewable filesystem. R2 holds large blobs. Brain captures durable decisions and reusable pattern learning after verification.

## 3. Use-case catalog by product/domain

### Research / knowledge work

#### Source-backed research reports

Shape:

```txt
WORK_ITEM_RECEIVED
→ fanoutSourceCollectors
→ extractClaims
→ verifyClaims
→ synthesize
→ publishReview
```

Events:

```txt
SOURCE_COLLECTED
CLAIM_EXTRACTED
CLAIM_VERIFIED
CLAIM_BLOCKED
SYNTHESIS_COMMITTED
WZRRD_PUBLISHED
```

Pi fit: context capsule pins prompt, source law, context pack, verifier contract. Worker sandboxes collect sources. Artifacts stores `sources.json`, source map, report, verifier result. Wzrrd/Brain review captures decisions.

Risks: stale sources, hallucinated claims, token burn. Use source caps, citation verifier, and budget cancel.

### Engineering

#### Code review

Shape:

```txt
checkout
→ fanoutReviewLanes
→ reduceFindings
→ verifyFindings
→ publishReview
→ optionalPatchGate
```

Risks: untrusted PR code, false positives, secret leakage. Default read-only sandboxes. Mutating patches require human gate.

#### Migrations/refactors

Shape:

```txt
inventory
→ sliceByCallsites
→ parallelPatchForks
→ testEach
→ mergeCandidate
→ adversarialReview
→ capture
```

Pi fit: Artifacts fork per slice. Supervisor owns merge policy. Verification contract pins expected tests/behavior.

Risks: merge conflicts, semantic drift, expensive test loops. Cap hot workers; serialize final merge.

#### Devtools / CI/CD

Shape:

```txt
forkArtifact
→ buildTest
→ preview
→ verify
→ publishStatus
→ cleanup
```

Pi fit: sandbox runs build/test. Artifacts stores worktree and receipts. Wzrrd exposes preview/test status.

Risks: runaway builds and untrusted code. Hard timeouts, no broad secrets, small container caps.

### Support / inbox

#### Support triage

Shape:

```txt
classify
→ fetchCustomerContext
→ draftOrAction
→ approvalWait
→ sendArchiveEscalate
```

Events:

```txt
THREAD_CLASSIFIED
CUSTOMER_CONTEXT_FETCHED
DRAFT_READY
HUMAN_APPROVED
REPLY_SENT
ESCALATED
```

Pi fit: capsule key = support thread. Secret lease grants narrow API access. Artifacts stores evidence/draft. Wzrrd/Brain handles tricky cases.

Risks: wrong refund/access action, privacy leaks, tone drift. Approval required for customer-facing mutations.

#### Personal inbox triage

Shape:

```txt
debounceThread
→ classify
→ group
→ retrieveHistory
→ archiveDraftEscalate
```

Risks: over-archiving important mail. Use confidence thresholds and human review bucket.

### Data / media

#### ETL / sync

Shape:

```txt
ingestBatch
→ normalize
→ validateSchema
→ load
→ reconcile
→ capture | dlq
```

Sources: [Dead Letter Queues · Cloudflare Queues docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/queues/configuration/dead-letter-queues/), [Delivery guarantees · Cloudflare Queues docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/queues/reference/delivery-guarantees/).

Risks: duplicate writes, downstream 429s, PII. Use idempotency keys, destination throttle, DLQ review.

#### Media processing

Shape:

```txt
uploadEvent
→ probe
→ transcodeExtract
→ aiDescribe
→ verifyOutputs
→ publish
```

Pi fit: sandbox runs FFmpeg/OCR/browser tools. R2 stores large blobs. Artifacts stores manifests, transcripts, thumbnails.

Risks: big files, egress, active container cost. Cap size/duration and queue slow jobs.

### Ops / security

#### Incident investigation

Shape:

```txt
dedupeAlert
→ investigateLogs
→ hypothesize
→ runSafeChecks
→ proposeFix
→ approveOrExecute
```

Risks: self-healing can make shit worse. Keep diagnosis read-only. Gate production mutation.

#### Security workflow

Shape:

```txt
enrichAlert
→ classifySeverity
→ parallelInvestigate
→ verifyRepro
→ recommendOrBlock
→ hitlAction
```

Risks: prompt injection, secret exposure, false containment. No privileged action from untrusted-reader lanes.

### Marketing / lifecycle

#### Marketing ops

Shape:

```txt
segment
→ enrich
→ generateVariants
→ approvalWait
→ send
→ measure
→ learn
```

Risks: spam/compliance/brand damage. Throttle per provider/list. Approval for outbound.

#### Customer success

Shape:

```txt
accountSnapshot
→ classifyNeed
→ draftPlan
→ approval
→ crmUpdate
→ followupWait
```

Risks: creepy personalization and accidental sends. Human gate for external comms.

### Evals / model routing

Shape:

```txt
generateCases
→ parallelRun
→ judgePanel
→ aggregate
→ decisionGate
```

Pi fit: context packs pin fixtures/rubrics. Artifacts stores runs/results. Wzrrd shows comparison.

Risks: judge bias, flaky tests, token inferno. Fixed fixtures, sample caps, stop when confidence is enough.

## 4. Cloudflare primitive mapping

| Primitive | Use in Pi workflow system | Keep out of it |
|---|---|---|
| Workers | Edge ingress, auth, routing, supervisor shell, bindings | Long-running Pi CLI work |
| Durable Objects | Per-capsule actor, lock, snapshot pointer, event coordination, cancel/progress | Global mega-coordinator |
| Workflows | Durable steps, retries, sleeps, `waitForEvent`, restart/terminate | Lifecycle truth without XState receipts |
| Queues | Admission buffer, retries, delays, DLQ | Exactly-once assumptions |
| Sandbox SDK | Disposable Linux compute for Pi/git/tests | Durable memory |
| Containers | Hot runtime pool behind sandboxes | Unlimited concurrency fantasy |
| Artifacts | Git-native plans, machines, harnesses, context packs, outputs, transcripts | Secrets |
| R2 | Large blobs: traces, screenshots, datasets, videos | Fine-grained lifecycle state |
| D1 | Queryable status/index/audit facets | High-write global event log without batching |
| KV | Read-heavy config/cache/manifests | Locks or lifecycle truth |
| Secrets Store | Small root/account secrets | Full OAuth blobs / dynamic lease broker by itself |
| Dynamic Workers | Generated validators/tool glue in isolates | Pi CLI/git/test runner substrate |

